    "## ``while`` loops"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "slideshow": {
     "slide_type": "slide"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "Similarly to other programming languages, Python also provides a ``while`` loop which is similar to a ``for`` loop, but where the number of iterations is defined by a condition rather than an iterator:\n",
    "\n",
    "    while condition:\n",
    "        # do something"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "slideshow": {
     "slide_type": "slide"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "For example, in the following example:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 100,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "1\n",
      "1.5\n",
      "2.25\n",
      "3.375\n",
      "5.0625\n",
      "7.59375\n",
      "Once the while loop has completed, a has the value 11.390625\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "a = 1\n",
    "while a < 10:\n",
    "    print(a)\n",
    "    a = a * 1.5\n",
    "print(\"Once the while loop has completed, a has the value\", a)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "the loop is executed until ``a`` is equal to or exceeds 10."
   ]
  },
